# Same as .gitignore, EXCEPT .env is deliberately NOT listed here.
#
# EAS Build uploads your project by respecting .gitignore — UNLESS this file
# exists, in which case EAS uses ONLY this file instead. Since .env holds the
# EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_*/SUPABASE_* keys the app needs at build time, and
# .env is gitignored (correctly — it shouldn't be committed), a plain `eas
# build` would silently ship an app with no Firebase/Supabase config and it
# would fail to connect to anything. This file exists purely to carve out
# that one exception for build uploads.
#
# For anything beyond a personal/demo build, prefer EAS's own Environment
# Variables (`eas env:set ...`) instead of this file — see
# https://docs.expo.dev/eas/environment-variables/

# dependencies
node_modules/

# Expo
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts

# Native
.kotlin/
*.orig.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision

# Metro
.metro-health-check*

# debug
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*

# macOS
.DS_Store
*.pem

# local env files (but NOT .env itself — see note above)
.env*.local

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

# generated native folders
/ios
/android
serviceAccountKey.json
scripts/seed-roster.js
scripts/seed-allowlist.js
scripts/seed-timetable.mjs
*.apk
build.log

scripts/serviceAccountKey.json.env
.firebase/